.TH FZF 1 "2026-11-08" "holyc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fzf \- interactive fuzzy finder, a one\-file C implementation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fzf
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads lines from standard input (or, when standard input is a terminal, from
.BR $FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND ),
lets you narrow them by typing and prints the selected lines. It follows the command line, the scoring
(FuzzyMatchV2), the extended search syntax and the default look of fzf 0.74. It needs only libc and pthreads.
Prefix a long option with
.B no\-
or use the \fB+\fR form of a short option to turn it off.
.SH OPTIONS
Matching:
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extended
extended search syntax (on by default)
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exact
exact matches instead of fuzzy
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case ", " \-\-smart\-case ", " \-\-literal
case handling and plain\-string matching
.TP
.BI \-\-scheme " default|path|history"
scoring scheme
.TP
.BI \-\-algo " v1|v2"
matching algorithm
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nth " \fIN[,..]\fR"
limit matching to these fields
.TP
.BI \-\-with\-nth " N[,..]"
transform the displayed lines
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delimiter " \fISTR\fR"
field delimiter (string or regex)
.TP
.BR \-\-tac ", " \-\-sort ", " \-\-tiebreak " \fIlist\fR, " \-\-disabled
result order and a mode that turns matching off
.TP
.BR \-\-track ", " \-\-id\-nth " \fIN\fR"
keep the cursor on the same item when the list changes
.PP
Interface:
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-query " \fISTR\fR"
start with this query
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-select\-1 ", " \-0 ", " \-\-exit\-0
accept automatically when exactly one item matches / exit when none does
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filter " \fISTR\fR"
non\-interactive: print the matches for STR and exit
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-multi [=\fIN\fR]
select several items (Tab to mark)
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-query ", " \-\-expect " \fIkeys\fR, " \-\-read0 ", " \-\-print0 ", " \-\-ansi ", " \-\-sync
input and output handling
.TP
.BR \-\-layout " \fIdefault|reverse|reverse\-list\fR, " \-\-reverse ", " \-\-height " \fIN[%]\fR, " \-\-min\-height " \fIN\fR"
placement
.TP
.BR \-\-border [=\fISTYLE\fR] ", " \-\-margin ", " \-\-padding ", " \-\-info " \fISTYLE\fR, " \-\-prompt ", " \-\-pointer ", " \-\-marker ", " \-\-header ", " \-\-header\-lines " \fIN\fR, " \-\-footer ", " \-\-no\-input ", " \-\-wrap ", " \-\-highlight\-line"
what is drawn
.TP
.BI \-\-color " THEME"
preset (dark, light, 16, temple, bw) and/or \fISLOT:colour\fR pairs
.TP
.BR \-\-history " \fIFILE\fR, " \-\-history\-size " \fIN\fR"
query history, Ctrl\-P and Ctrl\-N
.TP
.BR \-\-preview " \fICMD\fR, " \-\-preview\-window " \fIOPTS\fR, " \-\-preview\-label " \fISTR\fR, " \-\-no\-preview"
preview window; the command runs with the placeholders {}, {+}, {q}, {n}
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " KEY:ACTION[,..]"
key bindings; actions can be chained with \fB+\fR and include \fBreload\fR, \fBexecute\fR, \fBexecute\-silent\fR, \fBbecome\fR and \fBtransform*\fR. Events: start, load, change, focus, one, zero, result, multi, jump, resize
.TP
.BI \-\-hints[=N]
a key bar at the bottom (own extension, off with \fB\-\-no\-hints\fR)
.TP
.BI \-\-listen[=ADDR]
HTTP server: POST an action to run it, GET the state
.TP
.BI \-\-with\-shell " CMD"
shell used for commands
.TP
.BR \-\-mouse ", " \-\-cycle ", " \-\-keep\-right ", " \-\-scroll\-off " \fIN\fR, " \-\-hscroll ", " \-\-tabstop " \fIN\fR"
behaviour
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-\-version
usage and version
.PP
Accepted and ignored for compatibility: \-\-gap, \-\-tail, \-\-tmux, \-\-walker*, \-\-list\-border and the other per\-section borders, \-\-bash/\-\-zsh/\-\-fish (use the Go fzf for shell key bindings).
.SH KEYS
Defaults: Ctrl\-A/E line start/end, Ctrl\-B/F or Left/Right move, Alt\-B/F by word, Ctrl\-D delete, Ctrl\-H or Backspace erase, Ctrl\-W erase word, Ctrl\-U erase line, Ctrl\-Y yank,
Ctrl\-J/K/N/P or Up/Down move the cursor, PageUp/PageDown page, Shift\-Up/Down scroll the preview, Enter or double click accept, Ctrl\-C/G/Q or Esc abort, Ctrl\-L redraw, wheel scrolls.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND
command that supplies the items when standard input is a terminal; the default walks the current directory
.TP
.B FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS
options placed before those on the command line
.TP
.B FZF_THEME_FILE
theme file; default
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fzf/theme
or
.I ~/.config/fzf/theme
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
disable colours
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fzf/theme
one \fB\-\-color\fR value (preset name and/or slot:colour pairs, separated by commas or newlines); lines starting with # are comments. Shared by every tool built on this library
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 a selection was printed, 1 no match, 2 error (unknown option), 130 aborted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grep (1),
.I docs/fzf.md
in the holyc source
